   "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Trees Outside Forests Preference</title>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"sp-scheme\">\n{\n \"format\": \"sp-scheme-package\",\n \"spScheme\": \"2.0\",\n \"survey\": {\n  \"title\": \"Landscape Preference for Trees Outside Forests\",\n  \"description\": \"Faithful replication of the visual choice experiment of di Cristofaro, Sallustio, Sitzia, Marchetti & Lasserre (2020), Forests 11(7): 728. Six landscapes of the Molise region, Italy, along an urban-rural-natural gradient (L1 homogeneous urban, L2 heterogeneous urban, L3 homogeneous rural, L4 heterogeneous rural, L5 heterogeneous forest, L6 homogeneous forest) were photographed by the authors and edited with a raster graphics editor into three versions each: no trees outside forests (TOF), medium TOF cover (1.7% of the viewshed) and high TOF cover (3.4%). Participants rank the three versions of each landscape by preference, then rank the six medium-cover photos. Rankings are stored as arrays from most to least preferred. Analysis as in the paper: preference distributions (least, intermediate, most preferred) for each TOF level within each landscape, an overall score per photo (rank within the triplet times the rank of the landscape in the final sequence), chi-square tests between respondent groups (age, gender, inhabitants vs. visitors, in town vs. out of town), and relations between preference and landscape metrics. With 360 respondents intercepted in Molise, high TOF cover was most preferred in the urban landscapes (86.9% in L1, 72.8% in L2) and photos without TOF were least preferred in urban and rural landscapes, while in the natural landscapes high TOF cover was least preferred and the homogeneous forest landscape was most liked without TOF (62.5%). Differences from the original study: (1) the paper showed each triplet on A2 sheets in face-to-face interviews in public places of Molise, with quotas by age, gender, origin and residence; here the photos are shown on screen and anyone can take part; (2) the paper does not say how the photos were placed on the sheets, so each triplet is shown in the printed order (no, medium, high TOF) and the final six in order L1-L6; (3) participants tap photos from most to least preferred instead of writing 1-3 (least to most), and the ranks are stored from most to least preferred; (4) the paper names the personal questions (profession, education, marital status, age group, gender, inhabitant or visitor, home in town or out of town) but not their wording or answer options, which are ours; (5) the photos are the copies printed in Figure 2 (about 670 x 360 px).\",\n  \"locale\": \"en\",\n  \"mediaFolders\": [\"landscapes\"],\n  \"pages\": [\n   {\"name\": \"start\", \"elements\": [\n    {\"type\": \"consent\", \"name\": \"consent\", \"title\": \"I agree to take part. Participation is voluntary and my answers are recorded anonymously for research.\", \"isRequired\": true, \"labelTrue\": \"I agree\", \"labelFalse\": \"I do not agree\"}\n   ]},\n   {\"name\": \"about\", \"elements\": [\n    {\"type\": \"radiogroup\", \"name\": \"gender\", \"title\": \"Gender\", \"isRequired\": true, \"choices\": [{\"value\":\"female\",\"text\":\"Woman\"},{\"value\":\"male\",\"text\":\"Man\"},{\"value\":\"other\",\"text\":\"Other / prefer not to say\"}]},\n    {\"type\": \"radiogroup\", \"name\": \"age_group\", \"title\": \"Age\", \"isRequired\": true, \"choices\": [{\"value\":\"18-35\",\"text\":\"18–35 years\"},{\"value\":\"36-55\",\"text\":\"36–55 years\"},{\"value\":\"over55\",\"text\":\"Over 55 years\"}]},\n    {\"type\": \"radiogroup\", \"name\": \"origin\", \"title\": \"Do you live in this region, or are you visiting?\", \"isRequired\": true, \"choices\": [{\"value\":\"inhabitant\",\"text\":\"I live in this region\"},{\"value\":\"visitor\",\"text\":\"I am a visitor\"}]},\n    {\"type\": \"radiogroup\", \"name\": \"residence\", \"title\": \"Where is your home?\", \"isRequired\": true, \"choices\": [{\"value\":\"in_town\",\"text\":\"In town (urban or peri-urban district)\"},{\"value\":\"out_of_town\",\"text\":\"Out of town (rural area)\"}]},\n    {\"type\": \"text\", \"name\": \"profession\", \"title\": \"Profession\", \"isRequired\": true},\n    {\"type\": \"radiogroup\", \"name\": \"education\", \"title\": \"Highest completed education\", \"isRequired\": true, \"choices\": [{\"value\":\"primary\",\"text\":\"Primary school\"},{\"value\":\"lower_secondary\",\"text\":\"Lower secondary school\"},{\"value\":\"upper_secondary\",\"text\":\"Upper secondary school\"},{\"value\":\"university\",\"text\":\"University degree or higher\"}]},\n    {\"type\": \"radiogroup\", \"name\": \"marital_status\", \"title\": \"Marital status\", \"isRequired\": true, \"choices\": [{\"value\":\"single\",\"text\":\"Single\"},{\"value\":\"married\",\"text\":\"Married or living with a partner\"},{\"value\":\"separated_widowed\",\"text\":\"Separated, divorced or widowed\"}]}\n   ]},\n   {\"name\": \"triplets\", \"elements\": [\n    {\"type\": \"ranking\", \"name\": \"triplet_rank\", \"title\": \"Rank the three photos of this landscape from the one you like most to the one you like least.\", \"isRequired\": true, \"choices\": [{\"value\":\"none\",\"text\":\"No trees outside forests\"},{\"value\":\"med\",\"text\":\"Medium cover (1.7%)\"},{\"value\":\"high\",\"text\":\"High cover (3.4%)\"}], \"description\": \"Keyed by landscape (L1-L6); array from most to least preferred.\"}\n   ]},\n   {\"name\": \"sequence\", \"elements\": [\n    {\"type\": \"ranking\", \"name\": \"landscape_rank\", \"title\": \"Rank these six landscapes from the one you like most to the one you like least.\", \"isRequired\": true, \"choices\": [{\"value\":\"L1\",\"text\":\"L1 homogeneous urban\"},{\"value\":\"L2\",\"text\":\"L2 heterogeneous urban\"},{\"value\":\"L3\",\"text\":\"L3 homogeneous rural\"},{\"value\":\"L4\",\"text\":\"L4 heterogeneous rural\"},{\"value\":\"L5\",\"text\":\"L5 heterogeneous forest\"},{\"value\":\"L6\",\"text\":\"L6 homogeneous forest\"}], \"description\": \"The six medium-cover photos; array from most to least preferred.\"}\n   ]}\n  ]\n }\n}\n</script>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#f2f3ee;--card:#fff;--ink:#1c201b;--muted:#5b6258;--accent:#3f6a3a;--line:#d8dbd1;--warn:#b3261e;--sel:#e2ecdc}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 16px 40px}\nh1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 8px}h2{font-size:1.15rem;margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:16px;margin-top:14px}\n.btn{appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 20px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;background:var(--accent);color:#fff}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}\n.btn.ghost{background:transparent;color:var(--accent);border:1px solid var(--accent);margin-left:8px}\n.rk{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin-top:12px}\n.rk.six{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}\n.rk button{appearance:none;border:3px solid transparent;border-radius:12px;padding:0;background:#fff;cursor:pointer;position:relative;overflow:hidden}\n.rk img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}\n.rk .n{position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:var(--accent);color:#fff;border-radius:50%;width:34px;height:34px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem}\n.rk button.on{border-color:var(--accent)}\n.blk{margin-top:14px}.blk:first-child{margin-top:0}\n.blk.miss{outline:2px solid var(--warn);outline-offset:4px;border-radius:8px}\nlabel.opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;cursor:pointer}\nlabel.opt:has(input:checked){background:var(--sel);border-color:var(--accent)}\ninput.tx{font:inherit;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;width:100%;max-width:22em}\n.err{color:var(--warn);margin-top:8px;min-height:1.5em;line-height:1.5}\n.prog{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:4px}\n.credit{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px 24px;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}\n@media (max-width:700px){.rk,.rk.six{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}\n@media (max-width:420px){.rk{grid-template-columns:1fr}}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p>Loading…</p></main>\n<footer class=\"credit\">Photographs and design: di Cristofaro, Sallustio, Sitzia, Marchetti &amp; Lasserre (2020), Landscape Preference for Trees Outside Forests along an Urban–Rural–Natural Gradient, Forests 11(7): 728, Figure 2 (doi:10.3390/f11070728, CC BY 4.0).</footer>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var KEY='dicristofaro2020:state', LS=['L1','L2','L3','L4','L5','L6'], LV=['none','med','high'], BG=['gender','age_group','origin','residence','profession','education','marital_status'];\n  var app=document.getElementById('app'), Q={}, files={}, st=null;\n  function esc(s){return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;'}[c];});}\n  function err(m){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e){e.textContent=m||'';e.style.visibility='';}}\n  function hideErr(){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e&&!app.querySelector('.miss'))e.style.visibility='hidden';}\n  function ok(r){return !(r&&r.ok===false);}\n  function save(){try{localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(st));}catch(e){}}\n  function send(list,b,next){if(b)b.disabled=true;Promise.all(list).then(function(rs){var bad=rs.filter(function(r){return !ok(r);})[0];if(bad){if(b)b.disabled=false;return err(bad.error);}next();});}\n  function intro(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Which landscapes do you like most?</h1><p>This survey is about how trees and small woods outside forests (single trees, rows and small groups of trees in towns and farmland) affect how people like a landscape. After a few questions about you, you will see six landscapes, each in three versions, and put the versions in order of preference. At the end you will put six landscapes in order. It takes about 5 minutes.</p>'+\n     '<div class=\"card\"><label class=\"opt\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ok\"> '+esc(Q.consent.title)+'</label><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Start</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){if(!document.getElementById('ok').checked)return err('Consent is needed to continue.');\n      send([SPSite.answer('consent',true)],this,function(){st.step='about';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function about(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h2>About you</h2><div class=\"card\">'+BG.map(function(n){var q=Q[n];\n      if(q.type==='text')return '<div class=\"blk\" data-n=\"'+n+'\"><b>'+esc(q.title)+'</b><div><input class=\"tx\" type=\"text\" id=\"in_'+n+'\" value=\"'+esc((st.bg||{})[n]||'')+'\"></div></div>';\n      return '<div class=\"blk\" data-n=\"'+n+'\"><b>'+esc(q.title)+'</b>'+(q.choices||[]).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"'+n+'\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"'+((st.bg||{})[n]===c.value?' checked':'')+'> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div>';}).join('')+\n      '<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Continue</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){var L=[],miss=[],bg=st.bg||(st.bg={});\n      BG.forEach(function(n){var q=Q[n],el=app.querySelector('.blk[data-n=\"'+n+'\"]');\n        if(q.type==='text'){var raw=((document.getElementById('in_'+n)||{}).value||'').trim();if(raw){bg[n]=raw;L.push(SPSite.answer(n,raw));}else miss.push(el);return;}\n        var x=app.querySelector('input[name=\"'+n+'\"]:checked');if(!x){miss.push(el);return;}bg[n]=x.value;L.push(SPSite.answer(n,x.value));});\n      save();\n      if(miss.length){miss.forEach(function(el){el.classList.add('miss');});miss[0].scrollIntoView({block:'center'});return err('Please answer all seven questions.');}\n      send(L,this,function(){st.step='trip';st.k=0;save();route();});};\n  }\n  function rankPage(opts){\n    var pick=(opts.saved||[]).slice();\n    function draw(){\n      app.innerHTML='<div class=\"prog\">'+esc(opts.prog)+'</div><h2>'+esc(opts.head)+'</h2><p>'+esc(opts.help)+'</p><div class=\"rk'+(opts.items.length>3?' six':'')+'\">'+opts.items.map(function(it,i){var k=pick.indexOf(it.v);\n        return '<button type=\"button\" data-v=\"'+it.v+'\" class=\"'+(k>=0?'on':'')+'\"><img alt=\"Photo '+(i+1)+'\" src=\"'+esc(it.url)+'\">'+(k>=0?'<span class=\"n\">'+(k+1)+'</span>':'')+'</button>';}).join('')+\n        '</div><div class=\"card\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\"'+(pick.length<opts.items.length?' disabled':'')+'>Continue</button><button class=\"btn ghost\" id=\"clr\"'+(pick.length?'':' hidden')+'>Start again</button><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n      Array.prototype.forEach.call(app.querySelectorAll('[data-v]'),function(b){b.onclick=function(){var v=b.getAttribute('data-v'),k=pick.indexOf(v);if(k>=0)pick=pick.slice(0,k);else pick.push(v);opts.keep(pick);draw();};});\n      document.getElementById('clr').onclick=function(){pick=[];opts.keep(pick);draw();};\n      document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){if(pick.length<opts.items.length)return err('Please put all photos in order.');opts.done(pick.slice(),this);};\n    }\n    draw();\n  }\n  function trip(){\n    var k=st.k,L=LS[k];st.tr=st.tr||{};\n    rankPage({prog:'Landscape '+(k+1)+' of 6',head:'Put these three photos in order of preference',\n      help:'Tap the photo you like most first, then the next, then the one you like least. Tap a numbered photo again to undo from there.',\n      items:LV.map(function(v){return {v:v,url:files[L+'_'+v].url};}),saved:st.tr[L],\n      keep:function(p){st.tr[L]=p.slice();save();},\n      done:function(p,b){send([SPSite.answer('triplet_rank',p,{key:L,shown:LV.map(function(v){return files[L+'_'+v].name;})})],b,function(){if(k<5)st.k=k+1;else st.step='seq';save();route();});}});\n  }\n  function seq(){\n    rankPage({prog:'Last step',head:'Put these six landscapes in order of preference',\n      help:'Tap the landscape you like most first and the one you like least last. Tap a numbered photo again to undo from there.',\n      items:LS.map(function(L){return {v:L,url:files[L+'_med'].url};}),saved:st.sq,\n      keep:function(p){st.sq=p.slice();save();},\n      done:function(p,b){send([SPSite.answer('landscape_rank',p,{shown:LS.map(function(L){return files[L+'_med'].name;})})],b,function(){st.step='done';save();route();});}});\n  }\n  function finish(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Thank you!</h1><div class=\"card\"><p id=\"fin\">Submitting…</p><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    SPSite.complete().then(function(r){if(!ok(r)){err(r.error||'Some answers are missing.');setTimeout(function(){st.step='intro';save();route();},1800);}\n      else{try{localStorage.removeItem(KEY);}catch(e){}var s=document.getElementById('fin');if(s)s.textContent='Your answers are saved.';}});\n  }\n  app.addEventListener('change',function(e){var b=e.target.closest&&e.target.closest('.blk');if(b){b.classList.remove('miss');hideErr();}});\n  app.addEventListener('input',function(e){var b=e.target.closest&&e.target.closest('.blk');if(b){b.classList.remove('miss');hideErr();}});\n  function route(){var s=st.step;window.scrollTo(0,0);if(s==='about')return about();if(s==='trip')return trip();if(s==='seq')return seq();if(s==='done')return finish();intro();}\n  SPSite.onReady(function(ctx){\n    ['consent','triplet_rank','landscape_rank'].concat(BG).forEach(function(n){Q[n]=SPSite.getQuestion(n)||{};});\n    (SPSite.getMedia('landscapes')||[]).forEach(function(f){files[f.name.replace(/\\.[^.]+$/,'')]=f;});\n    var need=[];LS.forEach(function(L){LV.forEach(function(v){if(!files[L+'_'+v])need.push(L+'_'+v);});});\n    if(need.length){app.innerHTML='<h1>Images missing</h1><p>Upload '+esc(need.join(', '))+' (.jpg) to the media folder \"landscapes\".</p>';return;}\n    try{st=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY));}catch(e){st=null;}\n    var a=(ctx&&ctx.answers)||{};\n    if(!(st&&st.step)||a.consent!==true)st={step:'intro'};\n    save();route();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
   "version": "1.0",
